an't find child care  illinois governor jb pritzker has issued  child care workers one thousand dollar  bonuses and offered three months of free  care to parents looking for work if  we're not investing in our young  children we're creating a terrible  future for ourselves so it's an  investment in the future not just in  helping people get back to work so they  can pay their bills we have to stop  thinking about  things in one year increments  investing in young children means that  you're going to get a 20 30 40 year  return  illinois along with states like kansas  and tennessee are using relief funding  to reduce the amount low-income families  have to pay out-of-pocket michigan new  mexico and others are upping the amount  they reimburse providers for children  that receive government assistance more  plans are being announced each week with  the aid that's coming in we've gone in  and we're able to change certain things  update the hvac  change the flooring we're able to do  certain things to make sure that it's a  safer place for the kids new york has  given grants to providers like jasmine  corneal who is hoping to reopen one of  her three new york city child care  centers forced to close last year that  literally was like our lifeline the  programs are here they're here to  stabilize our industry  but the stabilization is supposed to be  for about six months and um this  pandemic is still going  and families still need  so  where do we go where do we go from here  in his buildback better plan president  biden proposes a massive spending  increase that would expand child care  access and cap costs my plan gets us  back on track  provides two years of high quality  preschool for every child in america the  biden plan remains stuck but growing  bipartisan recognition that help is  needed has priskar and others optimistic  what do you see as the future here for  states  once that federal money goes away we  need the federal government to step up  annually it can